; ==============================================================================
; pptx_playground.rgr — the API and the editor, in one page.
; ==============================================================================
;
; The playground writes a deck with the published API and then shows it in the
; EDITOR — not in a picture of one. That is the whole claim the page makes, and
; it only means anything if the two are the same build: a page that generated a
; deck with one copy of the code and drew it with another could show a slide
; that no reader would ever get.
;
; So one bundle holds all of it. `PptxWeb` is the viewer the standalone page
; already uses, unchanged; `PptxApi`, `PptxRenderer` and `PptxVega` are the
; published surface — the npm package splits those three into separate entry
; points so a caller carries only what they name, and a single page that
; offers all three has nothing to split. The
; page runs the reader's JavaScript against the second, takes the bytes it
; produces, and opens them in the first — which is exactly the round trip a
; caller makes when they write a deck and someone opens it in PowerPoint,
; except that here the reader watches it happen.
;
; Nothing is added to either side for the page's benefit. If the playground can
; draw it, the API produced it.
; ==============================================================================

Import "../pptx_web.rgr"
Import "../../api/PptxRenderApi.rgr"
Import "../../api/PptxChartApi.rgr"

class PptxPlayground {
    ; @internal The viewer, so the page can hand a generated deck straight to it.
    def viewer:PptxWeb (new PptxWeb)
    ; @internal The renderer, for the PNG and PDF buttons.
    def renderer:PptxRenderer (new PptxRenderer)

    Constructor () {
    }

    ; The faces this page must fetch, in the order the fallback walk takes
    ; them. Handed out rather than written into the HTML so the page and the
    ; desktop cannot disagree about which fonts a deck is measured in.
    sfn faces:[string] () {
        return (PptxRenderer.standardFaces())
    }
}
